* LM2937 bandgap reference - runnable ngspice testbench
* Source: mmo-chip Spectre export of the extracted LM2937 (see .tools/lm2937.cir)
* Converted to ngspice syntax by shared/spiceNetlist.
*
* The devices use generic placeholder models, so the numbers show the topology
* and the order of magnitude, not a sign-off of the real LM2937 process.
*
* Run:  ngspice -b lm2937_bandgap.cir
* Expected: v(ref) ~ 0.911 V (bandgap node), v(out) ~ 4.98 V, i(vdd) ~ -0.347 mA
*
* For a supply sweep replace the .op block below with:
*   .dc VDD 0 6 0.5
*   .measure dc vref_at_5v find v(ref) at=5
* (one analysis per netlist: ngspice keeps a single plot and drops the other)
* ngspice netlist
* LM2937 simplified netlist (from mmo-chip Spectre export)
* Q: C B E S model ; R: a b r ; D: a b ; C: a b c
* -- Model Cards --
.MODEL npn NPN (BF=200 IS=1e-16 VAF=50)
.MODEL pnp PNP (BF=100 IS=1e-16 VAF=50)
.MODEL diode D (IS=1e-14 N=1)

.subckt LM2937 OUT VCC GND ref ref_1 net230 net345234
